<p>China’s General Administration of Customs said exports rose 14.1% from a year earlier in April in U.S. dollar terms, reaching $359.44 billion, while imports increased 25.3% to $274.62 billion. The export gain exceeded forecasts cited by Bloomberg and Reuters and followed a 2.5% increase in March. China’s April trade surplus widened to about $84.8 billion, up from $51.13 billion in March. Customs released the data ahead of President Trump’s expected visit to Beijing next week for talks with Chinese President Xi Jinping, with trade tensions expected to be discussed. The articles cited the U.S.-Israeli war with Iran, disruption around the Strait of Hormuz and higher energy and shipping costs as pressures on trade. China’s exports to the United States rose 11.3% year on year in April after a 26.5% fall in March.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/4xo_9WR7cGyoaIS4X13UrbFdCMm0fEBOBGM9pjQOUJtMUG1_hdOCO2Xf8JmSEZpz2yHYHn0ZF-P1N1L5piy5ujetwAbHkkAxj7IV4la9OIzE1P7PRqrFdW4IKDH6b6LxNA4BzdrNiYe5HUVPZYPDrDkHk_agSxN8Ap6UYpk72wNtkc5C-QDhjt2bkpkJD1oKye2Nzg' alt='At the Beijing auto show in April, which featured hundreds of electric cars. Chinese electric vehicles are being exported in record numbers.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Yuan trade: In yuan terms, China’s total foreign trade reached 4.38 trillion yuan in April, up 14.2% year on year, with trade in the first four months totaling 16.23 trillion yuan.</li><li>Order rush: Reuters reported that factories moved to fill overseas orders as buyers stockpiled components over concerns that the Iran war could push input costs higher.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Financial Times: The robust trade surplus indicated that U.S. tariffs had done little to dent China’s manufacturing prowess. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/c1a18633-09d4-4875-878a-8a06c157a8ab'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>Economists surveyed by Bloomberg: The export increase topped the Bloomberg survey forecast of 8.4%, while import growth also beat the survey forecast of 20.0%. (<a href='https://www.malaymail.com/news/money/2026/05/09/china-exports-jump-141-pc-in-april-despite-global-war-driven-economic-pressure/219301'>Malay Mail</a>, <a href='https://www.mt.co.kr/world/2026/05/09/2026050913381928387'>Money Today</a>)</li><li>Economists cited by Reuters: Economists warned that a prolonged war and rising energy prices could weaken external demand, leaving sluggish domestic consumption unable to offset the loss. (<a href='https://www.brecorder.com/news/40420356/china-april-exports-rebound-strongly-after-sluggish-march-trade-surplus-widens'>Business Recorder</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/c1a18633-09d4-4875-878a-8a06c157a8ab'>China’s exports jump 14% ahead of Xi-Trump summit</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/china-april-exports-jump-141-year-ago-ahead-132804345'>China says April exports jump 14.1% from a year ago ahead of Trump-Xi summit</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/economy/economic-indicators/article/3352970/china-trade-growth-resilient-april-despite-hormuz-crisis-inflating-costs'>China defies Hormuz crisis with record monthly export value in April</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/09/business/china-april-trade-exports-imports.html'>China’s Exports and Imports Set Records in April Amid High Energy Costs</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/international-business/chinaa-trade-figures-exports-jump-14-1-in-april-ahead-of-trump-xi-visit/articleshow/130970793.cms'>China&#x27;a trade figures: Exports jump 14.1% in April, ahead of Trump-Xi visit</a> - indiatimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nationalheraldindia.com/international/china-says-exports-jump-14-percent-from-a-year-ago-ahead-of-trump-xi-jinping-summit'>China says exports jump 14.1 pc from a year ago ahead of Trump-Xi summit</a> - nationalheraldindia.com</li><li><a href='htt